                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4d7c67d4-8b8c-4805-9ca1-a1a97e01585f",
                        "source_entry_id": "1c0b2b93-7035-3440-b66d-50d43b0b465f",
                        "source_sense_id": "7176cb5d-3e43-365f-a809-9183c61eab6f",
                        "target_lang_word": "silently",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "silently",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "73db7210-4dfc-33b7-9d1d-a3d4c6c99ec3",
                                        "entry_id": "d3aaf0d9-85cb-3950-96cc-2596731d1cf1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a silent manner; making no noise."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9dd1de5e-2418-443b-bc85-8832823a89fa",
                                                "sense_id": "73db7210-4dfc-33b7-9d1d-a3d4c6c99ec3",
                                                "text": "It often happens that the most important results in the natural world are brought about by causes which operate silently, if not imperceptibly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db4e2e38-6298-4fab-afb0-ee64d924855e",
                                                "sense_id": "73db7210-4dfc-33b7-9d1d-a3d4c6c99ec3",
                                                "text": "Frederick, I presume, at this late hour of four, may be snatching a morsel of dinner; his orderlies are silently speeding, plans taken, orders given: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0c4f1bd-e3dd-3db0-ac81-e039fd2f4797",
                                        "entry_id": "d3aaf0d9-85cb-3950-96cc-2596731d1cf1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of an edit or change to a text, without explicit acknowledgment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f21bbce9-e5e9-401a-9362-d9bccc78bf57",
                                                "sense_id": "c0c4f1bd-e3dd-3db0-ac81-e039fd2f4797",
                                                "text": "There never was an English-language text, either in 1561 or 1859. Yule and Burnell have silently provided a translation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "40f2187b-f782-42f7-a3d7-0cdbcfa426c2",
                        "source_entry_id": "1c0b2b93-7035-3440-b66d-50d43b0b465f",
                        "source_sense_id": "7176cb5d-3e43-365f-a809-9183c61eab6f",
                        "target_lang_word": "tacitly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tacitly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f111e198-1621-353a-84e3-07362fcd7fd5",
                                        "entry_id": "da3237bc-0adc-3025-8255-9611b3da52fb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a tacit manner; done in silence or implied."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43c855a7-5594-490e-adca-57cd6ceb4000",
                                                "sense_id": "f111e198-1621-353a-84e3-07362fcd7fd5",
                                                "text": "Your failure to object to the request resulted in you tacitly approving the change."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ba137f2-530d-429d-83ad-7e5063616ee7",
                                                "sense_id": "f111e198-1621-353a-84e3-07362fcd7fd5",
                                                "text": "The new accusation brought by Urban against Manfred of murdering his sister-in-law's embassador – it may be observed that, tacitly, he acquits him of parricide, fratricide, and nepoticide – requires a little explanation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e5592a0-2a44-454f-b309-ebdfb87bd8e1",
                                                "sense_id": "f111e198-1621-353a-84e3-07362fcd7fd5",
                                                "text": "Since old Waziri’s death Tarzan had been directing the warriors in battle, and the temporary command had been tacitly conceded to him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c9e3986-58da-4bc9-b586-610c8ef0621c",
                                                "sense_id": "f111e198-1621-353a-84e3-07362fcd7fd5",
                                                "text": "The assumption that these are identical in meaning and usage between Indian English and Anglo-American English, while tacitly accepted, is untested, and fundamentally unknown."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5cc2ec04-1d8e-4076-b64a-03a97f5a6722",
                                                "sense_id": "f111e198-1621-353a-84e3-07362fcd7fd5",
                                                "text": "Regarding the “3.5% rule”, she [Erica Chenoweth] points out that while 3.5% is a small minority, such a level of active participation probably means many more people tacitly agree with the cause."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ea2277f4-6fea-4465-9848-a38d207cc82e",
                        "source_entry_id": "1c0b2b93-7035-3440-b66d-50d43b0b465f",
